SPARTA-GUI universal binaries for macOS (arm64/x86_64)
======================================================

This package provides a universal binary of SPARTA-GUI that runs natively
on both Apple Silicon (arm64) and Intel (x86_64) Macs running macOS version
12 (Monterey) or newer.

A universal build of the SPARTA shared library (libsparta) is bundled inside
the application, so SPARTA-GUI works out of the box: you do not need to
compile or install anything else.  A set of SPARTA example input decks is
also bundled and can be opened from the "File > Open Example" menu.

Installation
------------

Drag the SPARTA-GUI application onto the Applications folder icon in this
disk image window.

The first time you launch SPARTA-GUI, macOS may block it because it was
downloaded from the internet and is not signed by an identified developer.
To allow it to run, either:

  - right-click (or control-click) the SPARTA-GUI app and choose "Open",
    then confirm "Open" in the dialog, or

  - open "System Settings", go to "Privacy & Security", and click
    "Open Anyway" next to the message about "sparta-gui", or

  - run this once in the Terminal app:

        xattr -cr /Applications/SPARTA-GUI.app

Using your own SPARTA build (advanced)
--------------------------------------

If you have compiled your own version of SPARTA as a shared library (for
example to enable additional packages), you can tell SPARTA-GUI to load it
instead of the bundled one: open the Preferences dialog and set the path to
your libsparta shared library, or launch once from the Terminal with

    /Applications/SPARTA-GUI.app/Contents/MacOS/sparta-gui -p /path/to/libsparta.dylib

SPARTA-GUI stores the chosen library location in its preferences and reuses
it on the next launch.

Font size
---------

Depending on the size and resolution of your screen, the fonts may be too
small to read comfortably.  This can be adjusted by setting the environment
variable QT_FONT_DPI.  The default value is 72, so to increase the fonts by
a third, add the following line to your ~/.zprofile file:

    export QT_FONT_DPI=96
